            <div xml:id="d123">

                <pb facs="0220" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.73/28½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-25T13:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25, 1920—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>39. Department’s telegram December 22nd, 4 p.m.<anchor n="97" xml:id="d123-f1"/>
                    Under date of May 24th Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs has informed this
                    Embassy in a written memorandum that the Pernambuco-Monrovia cable is not in
                    operation. The personnel of company were not molested and the cable equipment
                    was not seized [during the] war. For the moment at least it is not the intention
                    of the Brazilian Government to utilize this cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
